WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.599 --> 00:00:06.839
We really can't talk about the Overton window
moves and creeping normality in 2019 without

00:00:06.839 --> 00:00:12.160
talking about how extreme right wing ideology
has become mainstreamed and is now part of

00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:16.790
what is considered legitimate political discourse
in way too many circles.

00:00:16.790 --> 00:00:21.570
There's a really good piece in the Guardian
about this by Mark Townsend and machine machinic

00:00:21.570 --> 00:00:26.310
ball that spells this out and it's something
I've been telling you for some time now and

00:00:26.310 --> 00:00:28.080
I encourage you to read the piece.

00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:34.280
The right in the United States has very successfully
pulled the discussion around a ton of political

00:00:34.280 --> 00:00:39.710
issues to the right and this is a huge structural
advantage for them because there are too many

00:00:39.710 --> 00:00:43.780
issues including abortion, immigration, and
many others.

00:00:43.780 --> 00:00:48.380
They are winning merely by pulling the discussion
to the extreme, right?

00:00:48.380 --> 00:00:51.690
The left has some wins on this in the United
States.

00:00:51.690 --> 00:00:58.019
So over the last two to three years we've
seen the left insert more progressive ideas

00:00:58.019 --> 00:01:00.260
into the mainstream discussion about healthcare.

00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:04.850
For example, everybody's talking now about
Medicare for all and other single payer systems.

00:01:04.850 --> 00:01:09.530
It doesn't mean we're necessarily about to
get them, but the debate has been pulled to

00:01:09.530 --> 00:01:14.409
the left on healthcare successfully by the
progressive movement inequality starting with

00:01:14.409 --> 00:01:15.729
occupy Wall Street.

00:01:15.729 --> 00:01:20.140
And since then with the likes of candidates
like Bernie Sanders and others, inequality

00:01:20.140 --> 00:01:22.340
has become mainstreamed as an issue.

00:01:22.340 --> 00:01:25.890
Taxation, more progressive ideas on taxation
for example.

00:01:25.890 --> 00:01:29.979
But the radicalization that comes from the
right is truly a danger.

00:01:29.979 --> 00:01:32.149
I'm going to give you a specific example.

00:01:32.149 --> 00:01:34.110
The idea of the great replacement.

00:01:34.110 --> 00:01:35.110
Okay.

00:01:35.110 --> 00:01:40.520
The great replacement is a right wing nationalist
conspiracy theory that officially started

00:01:40.520 --> 00:01:43.109
in France in 2012 by that name.

00:01:43.109 --> 00:01:47.210
But there are many versions of it and generally
it's the idea that White Christians are going

00:01:47.210 --> 00:01:52.789
to be replaced by non European people, Brown
people in many cases, sometimes not Christians.

00:01:52.789 --> 00:01:56.070
And it's going to destroy everything and it's
going to be terrible.

00:01:56.070 --> 00:02:02.319
And there are versions of this that date back
decades, hundreds of years, even longer.

00:02:02.319 --> 00:02:06.869
Uh, maybe, uh, I guess I'd have to think about
it without being called the great replacement,

00:02:06.869 --> 00:02:09.250
but the idea has been around for a long time.

00:02:09.250 --> 00:02:14.150
This fear of the other, the other is going
to come in and replace us and take our status

00:02:14.150 --> 00:02:18.510
in society and maybe take our a riches or
maybe take our women, right?

00:02:18.510 --> 00:02:22.400
I mean there's different versions of this
great replacement idea, but it has been used

00:02:22.400 --> 00:02:27.500
to stoke nationalist extremist ideas and it's
been around for a long time here in the United

00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:28.500
States.

00:02:28.500 --> 00:02:32.420
White nationalists and other right wingers
have been pushing this for years in relation

00:02:32.420 --> 00:02:34.380
specifically to immigration policy.

00:02:34.380 --> 00:02:39.350
And usually it relates to Latin American immigrants
and it has unfortunately become mainstream.

00:02:39.350 --> 00:02:41.270
They've succeeded at this.

00:02:41.270 --> 00:02:42.720
It's on Fox News all the time.

00:02:42.720 --> 00:02:45.740
It's not fringe websites that are talking
about this.

00:02:45.740 --> 00:02:50.240
It has infected what is considered mainstream,
right wing political thinking.

00:02:50.240 --> 00:02:57.100
Fox News host, Laura Ingram did a segment
in August, which we covered basically a sanitized,

00:02:57.100 --> 00:03:02.200
great replacement segment about legal and
illegal immigrants forcing demographic change

00:03:02.200 --> 00:03:05.550
in the United States and destroying the country
by doing it.

00:03:05.550 --> 00:03:10.760
Tucker Carlson on Fox News, very similar thing,
numerous segments.

00:03:10.760 --> 00:03:17.290
One in which he said that Brown people coming
to the United States legally becoming citizens

00:03:17.290 --> 00:03:20.730
and voting in elections is a form of election
hacking.

00:03:20.730 --> 00:03:25.500
This is a fundamentally, it's a replacement
sort of conspiracy theory.

00:03:25.500 --> 00:03:31.400
Another segment in which Tucker Carlson ranted
about immigrants making our country dirtier.

00:03:31.400 --> 00:03:36.980
This type of discussion at one point was not
considered serious conversation on these issues.

00:03:36.980 --> 00:03:42.140
I still would have disagreed with what the
right thought at the time, but they were not

00:03:42.140 --> 00:03:46.040
overtly radical in this particular way that
I'm showing you.

00:03:46.040 --> 00:03:51.870
The Institute for Strategic Dialogue has been
studying this and they found that these formerly

00:03:51.870 --> 00:03:54.590
sort of obscure ideas are now everywhere.

00:03:54.590 --> 00:03:57.840
Donald Trump references them in speeches on
Twitter.

00:03:57.840 --> 00:04:00.970
It's happening in European countries among
the nationalist parties.

00:04:00.970 --> 00:04:05.030
It's all over social media, particularly on
Twitter, even outside of the president's own

00:04:05.030 --> 00:04:06.030
tweets.

00:04:06.030 --> 00:04:11.050
The right likes to say that there's left wing
bias just implicit in all of our discussions

00:04:11.050 --> 00:04:16.590
and on media and they love the example of
Twitter is left wing because if you miss gender,

00:04:16.590 --> 00:04:19.690
people on purpose you could get banned.

00:04:19.690 --> 00:04:26.210
This is a joke compared to the reality that
straight up xenophobic, almost friend knowledgist

00:04:26.210 --> 00:04:27.210
type trash.

00:04:27.210 --> 00:04:28.210
Look that up.

00:04:28.210 --> 00:04:31.800
If you don't remember what that is is now
part of the discussion around many of these

00:04:31.800 --> 00:04:32.800
issues.

00:04:32.800 --> 00:04:33.970
They have slick branding.

00:04:33.970 --> 00:04:37.720
They come up with wording that makes it sound
relatively innocuous if you're not paying

00:04:37.720 --> 00:04:43.530
close enough attention, but they are pushing
extreme ideas into the gray area of valid

00:04:43.530 --> 00:04:48.230
political discussion and it has the effect
that is beneficial for them of pulling the

00:04:48.230 --> 00:04:51.970
Overton window seriously to the right, the
right slick.

00:04:51.970 --> 00:04:56.610
A branding has pushed extreme right wing ideas
into mainstream discourse.

00:04:56.610 --> 00:05:01.490
They've successfully integrated them into
even corporate media discussions of many political

00:05:01.490 --> 00:05:06.610
issues while at the same time continuing to
shout that there's inherent left wing bias

00:05:06.610 --> 00:05:08.900
in all media and social platforms.

00:05:08.900 --> 00:05:15.139
This is one of the most successful disinformation
campaigns of the last 30 years and what we

00:05:15.139 --> 00:05:21.450
all need to understand is that even if the
craziest ideas that they espouse aren't made

00:05:21.450 --> 00:05:24.680
into reality, they're not made into policy.

00:05:24.680 --> 00:05:27.389
It makes the marginally less crazy.

00:05:27.389 --> 00:05:31.320
Ideas seem middle of the road in comparison.

00:05:31.320 --> 00:05:36.310
And that's the danger of the mainstreaming
of extremist nationalists, right wing ideas

00:05:36.310 --> 00:05:40.410
of the Overton window being pushed to the
right and if the creeping normalization that

00:05:40.410 --> 00:05:44.280
we've experienced over the last 15 years,
but particularly over the last year,

00:05:44.280 --> 00:05:45.940
two and a half under Donald Trump.

00:05:45.940 --> 00:05:47.639
I want to hear from you about this.

00:05:47.639 --> 00:05:51.040
Do you agree with my assessment and how do
you think we fight it?

